WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.787
Reading the output is
where the rules turn real.

2
00:00:02.787 --> 00:00:05.343
Six accounts are proposed for retirement,

3
00:00:05.343 --> 00:00:08.263
the orphans and the disabled
ones from Chapter 2.

4
00:00:08.263 --> 00:00:12.211
Others go to delegated or group
managed accounts, some are kept,

5
00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:16.312
and one app has no proposal because
nobody recorded where it runs.

6
00:00:16.312 --> 00:00:20.269
The findings tell the story: a
high-risk account scheduled too late,

7
00:00:20.269 --> 00:00:24.370
a Kerberos account kept with no
owner for its service principal name,

8
00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.320
an owner who overrode the
matrix but gave a reason,

9
00:00:27.320 --> 00:00:32.280
and two apps on the licensing list that
Conditional Access can't actually protect.
